# PDF Batch Agent

A lightweight web app for uploading many PDFs and converting them into Excel or text-based outputs for bulk processing.

## What it does

- Upload hundreds of PDF files in a single batch
- Extract text from each PDF page
- Export one Excel workbook per PDF
- Optionally combine them into a summary workbook
- Produce a ZIP archive with all generated files
- Optional OCR mode for scanned or image-based PDFs

## Tech stack

- Node.js + Express
- PDF.js for PDF text extraction
- Tesseract.js for OCR fallback
- XLSX for Excel generation
- Archive generation for batching downloads

## Getting started

```bash
npm install
npm start
```

Then open:

```text
http://localhost:3000
```

## Important note

This is a production-friendly starter implementation. For very large workflows (200–500 PDFs), the app is intentionally designed around a queued processing model and chunked batch handling. Real-world throughput depends on CPU, memory, and PDF complexity.

## Example use cases

- Convert vendor PDFs into Excel tables
- Extract data from scanned statements
- Batch process invoices, forms, and reports
- Generate a ZIP archive for final delivery

## Future upgrades

- Real table detection
- Better OCR accuracy for scanned files
- Cloud job queue (Redis + worker pods)
- S3 storage integration
- Authentication and dashboard
- Multi-user architecture

